travelers.prompt:
Use case: style-transfer / complete visual redesign.
Image 1 is the EDIT TARGET, used ONLY for its sixteen-cell order and the open-front U-shaped mouths. Discard its ornate architecture, materials and rendering completely.
Image 2 is the OFFICIAL STUDIO GHIBLI FRAME used ONLY as a STYLE reference: study the character's very clean fine dark-brown animation lines, large quiet flat color areas, simple restrained shadow shapes, and the separation between clean animation cels and painted backgrounds. Do not copy its character, costume, room, hats or composition.

REMAKE THE WHOLE FIRST IMAGE IN AN UNMISTAKABLE STUDIO GHIBLI HAND-DRAWN CEL-ANIMATION LOOK. These are original foreground animation characters, not Western fantasy illustrations, not detailed watercolor miniatures, not an isometric RPG asset pack, not 3D renders. Each city must look simple enough that an animator could redraw it on every frame: clean thin brown lineart, large matte flat fills, one gentle shadow tone per material, no gradients or specular highlights on metal, no watercolor grain on the foreground characters, no tiny ornamental detail. Absolutely NO gilded palaces, golden trim, shiny gems, individual brick outlines, ornate gears, decorative spires, hundreds of roof tiles, filigree, photorealistic texture or plastic bevels. Use humble off-white plaster, warm brown wood, faded slate-grey / blue-grey / moss-green roofs, soft muted red accents and a few broad patches of leaves.

The sixteen subjects are original friendly living traveling HOMES / FOREST COMPANIONS, organic and asymmetrical, not grand European castles. Give them a few readable features only: two large warm window-eyes, one crooked chimney, chunky wooden or earthen side feet, a small simple flag or plant. Mature forms may have 3 to 5 simple roof masses, never a miniature palace. Near-isometric three-quarter front view remains consistent for the game. They should feel gentle, curious, resourceful and alive.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS: one real transparent PNG atlas, EXACTLY four equal columns and four equal rows, sixteen complete isolated designs. Clear transparent gutters. No grid lines, labels, names, letters, numbers, logos, background scenery, paper rectangles, ground tiles or cast shadows.
EVERY city must remain an OPEN FRONT U / CRESCENT: rear house body plus left/right short arms curving forward. In every equal cell keep a large EMPTY TRANSPARENT mouth centered about x=.51, y=.80, horizontal radius .24, vertical radius .145, open to the lower front. No floor, courtyard, grass, wood planks, bridge, painted black disk, creature face or body may fill that mouth. All feet and structures stay outside the central empty opening.

EXACT ORDER:
ROW 1, growth stages:
0 a baby traveling cottage, one squat off-white house with grey-brown slanted roof, two large window-eyes, crooked chimney, simple crescent wooden side feet;
1 a young two-storey traveling home, two roof masses and a little side porch, soft blue-grey roof;
2 a medium village companion, three asymmetrical little houses / broad roof masses and one potted bush;
3 a mature traveling home, four or five simple roofs, a pair of chimneys, broad wooden side fins and stubby outer feet. All keep the same empty U mouth.

ROW 2, weapon personalities:
4 cannon home: rustic house plus two SHORT DARK IRON OR WOOD-AND-IRON CANNONS on the front left and front right outer arms, matte charcoal barrels, no brass armor;
5 frost garden home: off-white cottage with pale blue glass / ice roof planes and a few soft blue flowers, only one simple ice point;
6 wind-sail home: rustic little home with one broad cloth sail and a simple wooden windmill, faded sea-green / cream cloth;
7 lightning home: humble grey-roof cottage with two plain copper wire antennae and one matte pale-blue electrical bulb, not a jeweled palace.

ROW 3:
8 phoenix hearth home: a warm terracotta cooking-hearth house, a simple orange bird-shaped weather vane and a chimney;
9 cannon-wind home: two matte side cannons, a broad faded sail and a small wooden propeller;
10 cannon-frost home: two matte side cannons with simple pale-blue greenhouse roof shapes;
11 frost-wind home: soft pale-grey sail, simple cool-blue roof, a small patch of blue flowers.

ROW 4:
12 thunderheart cannon home: two readable matte side cannons and one simple blue electrical bulb tower on a warm wooden house;
13 sunforge sail home: simple hearth house with a warm ochre cloth sail and a small orange bird-shaped vane;
14 star-night home: a quiet indigo-roof dwelling with two warm window-eyes, a crescent sign and two small star lanterns, no ornate astronomy machine;
15 overclock home: a slightly lopsided cream wooden house with ONE plain round clock and a large simple winding key.

All sixteen must share the exact same restrained Studio Ghibli-style cel-animation linework and flat-paint treatment. The reference foreground character's clean animation finish is the target, NOT the detailed painted background. Keep all mouth centers transparent. No existing copyrighted character or recognizable existing film castle.
